# Phase-4 replay archive — block break: the first-writer-wins arbitration.
# G1's applied air-write is recorded, so its break (the drops carrier) is the
# first writer and the host accepts it exactly once: the drops register in
# the authoritative item table and the break relays to the other guest.
# G2's same-cell break has no record (its own air-write would have been
# refused as already-broken) — its drops come back as one ItemReject.
#
# Fossil of: BlockBreakSimulationTests.FirstBreak_AcceptedAndRelayed_RepeatRefused
# Mechanism: BlockBreakArbitration.TryAccept (one-shot per sender/cell),
#            ItemService.FireBlockDropsReceived / SendItemReject
#            (Runtime/Session/World/BlockBreakArbitration.cs)

@0 airwrite g1 5 7
@0 break g1 5 7 drops=77:ore
@0 break g2 5 7 drops=88:ore
@33 expect block_accepted 1 within 500
@33 expect block_accepted_by g1 1
@33 expect block_received g2 BlockDamaged 1
@33 expect block_reject g2 ItemReject 1
@33 expect block_registered 77
